1
00:00:00,091 --> 00:00:02,630
On paper, Rana's life looked nothing like

2
00:00:02,643 --> 00:00:03,437
a terrorist's.

3
00:00:03,893 --> 00:00:05,859
He came from a respectable family:

4
00:00:06,576 --> 00:00:08,763
one brother became a psychiatrist in the

5
00:00:08,763 --> 00:00:11,745
Pakistan military, another a journalist in

6
00:00:11,758 --> 00:00:12,279
Canada.

7
00:00:12,695 --> 00:00:14,258
He trained as a doctor.

8
00:00:14,688 --> 00:00:17,240
He served as a Captain in the Pakistan

9
00:00:17,240 --> 00:00:18,451
Army Medical Corps.

10
00:00:18,867 --> 00:00:21,771
Then, in the late 1990s, he deserted.

11
00:00:23,054 --> 00:00:24,903
The reasons are still unclear.

12
00:00:26,071 --> 00:00:29,118
In 1997 he emigrated to Canada with his

13
00:00:29,131 --> 00:00:30,967
wife, also a physician.

14
00:00:31,397 --> 00:00:34,157
Records show both became Canadian citizens

15
00:00:34,170 --> 00:00:35,238
in 2001.

16
00:00:35,654 --> 00:00:38,089
From Toronto, he moved into business and

17
00:00:38,102 --> 00:00:39,365
settled in Chicago.

18
00:00:39,769 --> 00:00:41,618
There was a halal meat business on

19
00:00:41,631 --> 00:00:42,490
Devon Avenue.

20
00:00:42,907 --> 00:00:44,678
And there was First World Immigration

21
00:00:44,691 --> 00:00:47,503
Services — offices across North America

22
00:00:47,516 --> 00:00:49,886
and, eventually, a branch in Mumbai.

23
00:00:51,033 --> 00:00:53,429
It was a real business, with real clients.

24
00:00:54,702 --> 00:00:56,981
That is exactly what made it useful.

